  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jazz Chisholm Jr. broke a 1\u20131 tie in the eighth and they held on tight.",
    "what_this_means": "The pitching held. Yarbrough took it to 2.2 clean innings before handing it to a parade of arms. Blackburn, Headrick, Cruz, Bednar. Who combined for 5.4 scoreless frames. The offense did almost nothing until it mattered. Eleven runners left on base, one run driven in across all those at-bats. That is the margin between a one-run win and a one-run loss. Chisholm's home run was the only conversion that landed. This is a team that survives on precision, not volume. When the pitching works this hard, the bats have to finish what's left. They did. Barely.",
    "what_to_watch": "Braxton Ashcraft takes the mound tonight for Pittsburgh with a 3.49 ERA. A test for a Yankees lineup that struck out nine times yesterday and hasn't found consistent rhythm. Ryan Weathers starts for New York in what shapes as another pitcher's duel in a division race where every half-game matters.",
